<title>SPAIN: Santander cuts prime by 25 bps to 7.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Santander cuts prime by 25 bps to 7.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Santander said on Friday it cut is prime by 25 basis points to seven percent.</p>
<p>The move followed the Bank of Spain's decision to cut its key rate by 25 basis points to 5.25 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
